will be taking this course on computer networks. So, we will be having about 40 lectures in

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:10.100
the series. So, today we will start with an introductory lecture which is about the

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:18.120
emergence of computer networks at brief history and a little bit about the protocols and

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.060
reference models which is an abstract view of computer networks.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:34.710
The textbooks for the course will be these three computer networking, a top down approach

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:42.430
featuring internet that is one by Kurov, data and computer communication by William

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:50.910
Stolling and computer networks by A.S. Stanenbaum. So, some of the material that we will be covering

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:56.190
here verbally as well as in the slide will be from these books.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:09.260
Now the first question is what is a computer network? So, a computer network is a number

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:16.060
of computers also known as nodes connected by some communication lines. So, we have these

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:23.320
computers which are connected by some communication lines. So, two computers connected to the

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:29.200
network can communicate with each other through other nodes if they are not directly connected

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:36.660
which means that computer does not have to be connected to all the other computers in

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:42.840
the network in order to communicate with any of them. It may be an indirect communication

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:51.800
via some other computer and the other point is that these nodes they are computers, but

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:57.860
some of them are not computers, some of them are sort of network devices. Now there are

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:04.720
various kinds of network devices like switches, routers, etcetera. So, they could also, so

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:09.360
they facilitate the communication and running of this entire network. So, they are also

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:17.440
taken as nodes in the network. So, finally we have some of the nodes, some nodes which

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:24.380
may be either computers or there may be network devices like switches and routers and there

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:34.820
is a communication between them. This communication of course can be of various types we will

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:42.420
come to that presently. So, the computers can communicate with each other. Now what do they

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:48.300
communicate? They exchange information between different computers. Now this information could

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:56.860
be of any kind of information. They could be data used by a program or they could be

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:03.880
some program itself or it could be any kind of information really. So, that is one

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:11.240
of the basic and major use of computer network. Of course, there are other specialized uses

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:18.500
of computer network. For example, interconnected small computers can replace a large computer.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:25.960
For example, you have a very large computation to perform and so further either you need

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:30.680
a very powerful and very large computer which may be costly. The other option could

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:37.280
be that you break up this work into very small pieces and assign them to the small computer.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:45.180
So, the small computers sort of do the computation on that small chunk of the problem and then

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:53.600
they communicate with each other to form the final solution. Then the other uses computer

00:04:54.120 --> 00:05:01.440
network which is coming into Vogue very much these days is that you can use this network

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:09.240
as a communication tool. We know the very basic say for example, you send emails to I mean

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:14.500
you can send emails to almost anybody these days and that is really a very cheap and

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:20.000
very fast mode of communication. Secondly, the computer network could also be used

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:28.640
for direct communication like say you could have communicate through voice over a computer

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:34.180
network, you can communicate through video over a computer network. So, all these different

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:40.900
communication is converging into this computer network and as a matter of fact nowadays when

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:47.100
we talk about the network we do not look upon it just as a computer network as a

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:54.900
matter of fact it is the bedrock on which say all this computing communication all

00:05:54.900 --> 00:06:02.820
these are converging and then of course, you have some application which are necessarily

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:10.980
of distributed nature. For example, let us say railway reservation system now obviously

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:18.220
even if you had a large computer to handle all the railway reservations in the world

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:23.760
in one place, but you would not want all the people to go to one place and sort

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:30.380
of form a huge queue. So, you want to distribute this functionality that means, for that of booking

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:36.440
ticket all over the country and that is what we do. So, these are sort of examples of

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:40.440
distributed system. So, this is a distributed reservation system. Similarly, there could

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:44.940
be other kinds of distributed system, there could be distributed databases and all

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:50.420
kinds of applications. So, that is the other application of networks.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:07:07.000
Now, a quick look at the history of this computers first and then we will sort of focus on computer

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:14.000
network. Well, in 1948 we have the first commercial computer installed it was an

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:23.360
Univac that was a big company once upon a time and then in 1958 the first US communication

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:30.680
satellite became operational. So, you see the network always has these two components

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:34.900
one is that you have to have this computer and then you have to have this communication

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:42.760
channel and satellite communication is of course, one of an important medium of communication

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:51.700
then in 1964 we have an airline reservation system which uses some kind of a packet switching

00:07:51.700 --> 00:08:01.160
network it was proposed by the RAND Corporation and in 1969 ARPANET the first packet switching

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:08.200
network began its operation. This was actually a watershed event as we will see this had

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:12.540
very far reaching impact on the way computer networks developed.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:21.860
Then in 1971 we have the first computer chip previous computers were made through very low

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:29.800
level gates and all, but the first 4 bit small computer chip with 2300 transistors and they

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:38.660
became available in 1971. In 1972 Ethernet specifications were formulated. Now, this

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:47.840
Ethernet is one protocol so to say. So, we will talk about protocols and different kinds

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:54.080
of protocols and Ethernet remains one of the most important network protocols that we

00:08:54.080 --> 00:09:03.360
use. So, that was first formulated in 1972. In 1974 IBM introduced its own version of

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:12.720
network in SNA. Then in 1975 Altair 8800 first commercial microcomputer that was sold as a

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:20.480
kit. So, we are actually looking at the very brief history of computers in general. So, in

