we see today almost everywhere. It was basically it started from Apple computers.

00:09:52.380 --> 00:10:00.820
In 1979 we had the VC calc as the first commercial spreadsheet. So, that is a very popular application

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:10.520
of computer these days. In 1981 IBM introduced IBM PC on with one floppy drive. Later on they

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:19.200
changed it with a drive and a hard drive also. And in 1983 TCP IP. So, this TCP IP

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:28.080
is another network protocol that we are using. Actually we use both Ethernet and TCP IP. So,

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:32.780
we actually we have different protocols which are running on the network we require and

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:38.280
how these different protocols are arranged and how they are used that I will cover today

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:42.640
in the second part of the lecture. So, this TCP IP is another important protocol

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:48.080
that is still very much different today that became the official protocol of ARPANET.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:55.600
Remember ARPANET we talked about that is a network which was set up in USA under DRDO and

00:10:55.600 --> 00:11:01.900
which had a very far reaching impact on the way network developed. In 1984 Apple introduced

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:13.860
GUI with Apple Macintosh and 1986 we see the first laptop PCs 88. So, IBM gives a multitasking

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:22.900
OS for the PCs. 1989 Microsoft releases Windows which is another multitasking system in that

